PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION: This commanding triptych by contemporary artist Shahin Zonoozi presents the vaunted Ferrari F40 with a contemporary minimalism that honors the purity of the supercar's design. Set against a saturated color field, the F40 appears almost suspended, its aggressive stance and unmistakable profile with sharp, aerodynamic lines distilled into a powerful graphic. Zonoozi’s disciplined brushwork and precise highlights reflect an engineer’s attention to structure, while his bold use of negative space situates the subject firmly within the language of modern fine art. “I wanted to honor the F40’s uncompromising form by isolating it within a bold color field,” Zonoozi says. “The triptych structure creates a sense of ceremony around the machine—an object of myth, engineering, and obsession.” Each of the three panels measures 36 inches by 48 inches for a combined measurement of 9 feet by 4 feet., All proceeds of the sale will go to Genius Garage, a 501c3 nonprofit educational charity that develops hands-on skills and provides practical work experience in aerospace, racing, automotive design, and social media content creation for a select group of college students. For more information, please visit the website, .

LOT_SUMMARY: Acrylic on canvas in three panels, Depicts the Ferrari F40 through contemporary minimalism, All proceeds go to Genius Garage, a 501c3 nonprofit educational charity, 9 × 4 ft. (each panel is 36 × 48 in.)

