PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION: Celebrating Ferrari’s relentless pursuit of performance, the Scuderia Spider 16M takes its name from Maranello’s 16th Formula 1 Constructors’ Championship—an achievement unrivaled in motor sports. Ferrari forged its reputation through racing triumphs, so it is only fitting that one of the company’s finest modern creations honor its success at the highest level of racing., Built in a limited series of just 499 examples, the Scuderia Spider 16M derives from Ferrari’s uncompromising F430 Scuderia. The exclusively open-top 16M retains the latter’s potent 4.3-liter V-8 but adds subtle refinements, including redesigned pistons and a higher compression ratio. The result is an engine that climbs to redline with thrilling immediacy, delivering torque and roar in equal measure. Rated by Ferrari at 503 horsepower and paired with its acclaimed F1-SuperFast2 six-speed transmission, the engine delivers scorching acceleration, sprinting from 0 to 60 mph in just 3.8 seconds and topping out at 196 mph., Despite the structural reinforcements required for its open-top design, the 16M remains astonishingly light, a testament to Ferrari’s relentless pursuit of weight reduction. Engineers implemented a comprehensive diet, which included lightened front and rear bumpers, reworked front suspension and steering, forged alloy wheels unique to the model, a carbon fiber roll bar, and titanium wheel bolts. Through these measures, the 16M sheds a remarkable 176 pounds compared to the standard F430 Spider, preserving the dynamic experience of the F430 Scuderia while delivering the thrill of open-air driving., Showing just 3,186 miles at cataloguing, this Scuderia Spider shines in Rosso Corsa with an Italian flag racing livery over Nero leather accented with Rosso Corsa stitching and technical fabric inserts. A copy of its window sticker shows it was sold new via Scottsdale Ferrari in Arizona, equipped with red brake calipers, carbon-fiber seats, Cavallino-embossed headrests, Scuderia fender shields, and the tricolor Italian flag applique., Benefiting from attentive stewardship, this Scuderia Spider had service work performed by authorized Ferrari dealers. In August 2025, Ferrari of San Antonio, Texas, carried out a comprehensive $14,712 inspection and service, which included repairing sticky buttons and installing new Michelin Pilot Sport tires. In December 2025, further inspection and servicing at Ferrari of Newport Beach, California, encompassed new drive belts, fluids, filters, gaskets, spark plugs, and battery. In sum, this meticulous attention ensures the car is poised to deliver its full measure of performance and exhilaration to the next fortunate custodian. The car is accompanied by its factory-issued 16GB iPod Touch, owner's books, and service records., A masterful blend of Formula 1 technology and open-air ferocity, the Scuderia Spider 16M awakens the senses through every twist and turn, delivering a visceral thrill that every true, must experience.

LOT_SUMMARY: A masterful blend of Formula 1 technology and open-air ferocity, One of just 499 built to celebrate Ferrari’s 16th Formula 1 World Championship Constructors’ title, Displaying just 3,186 miles at cataloguing time, Over $20,000 in servicing carried out in 2025 by Ferrari of San Antonio and Ferrari of Newport Beach, Finished in Rosso Corsa with Italian flag racing livery over Nero leather and Rosso Corsa stitching, Accompanied by factory-issued 16GB iPod Touch, owner's books, and service records

